/-- **The `j ≥ 2` half of the level-by-level graded step of the `p = 2` correction**
(Schmidt–Wingberg Step 1, clause (B) at `p = 2`).

For a finite group `G`, an involution `δ ∈ G` with `δ ≠ 1`, `n ∈ ℕ`, and every `σ = (i,j)` with
`2 ≤ j ≤ i`: every element `c` of the kernel of `Q_{σ+1} = F(n)/F(n)^{(σ+1)} → Q_σ = F(n)/F(n)^{(σ)}`
which is anti-fixed under the induced action of `δ` is a `δ`-difference *in the ambient group*
`Q_{σ+1}`, i.e. `c = (δ • e)⁻¹ * e` for some `e ∈ Q_{σ+1}`.

The kernel is the graded piece `E(σ) = F(n)^{(σ)}/F(n)^{(σ)+1}`, which by Proposition 5
(`Work.SSGRoute.prop5Data_exists`, the `G`-equivariant surjection `θ_σ` on the `j`-th tensor power of
`F(n)/F(n)^2`) is generated by the images of the "weight-`j` monomials".  The witness `e` must have a
`δ`-invariant exponent vector modulo `F(n)/F(n)^2` (otherwise its norm cannot land in the graded
piece at all), and then it is the "half" of the monomial: for the `δ`-orbit pair `{x, δx}` the class
of `(δ(x·δx))⁻¹(x·δx) = [x, δx]` is exactly the corresponding generator; for a general monomial the
error terms are commutators of strictly higher weight and die in the ambient group `Q_{σ+1}`, because
`[F(n)_i, F(n)] ⊆ F(n)_{i+1} ⊆ F(n)^{(σ+1)}` (this is `Work.SSGRoute.flowQuotSucc_ker_central`).

This is a strict piece of `Work.SSGRoute.gradedStep_general` (the `j = 1` pieces being
`Work.SSGRoute.gradedStep_j_one`), and it is exactly the shape of the family `GradedStep` of
`Submission/Work/SSGRoute/two_torsion_assembly.lean`.  The *strong* form, with the witness required
to lie in `E(σ)` itself, is FALSE (for `σ = (2,2)`, `n = 1`, `G = ℤ/2` the graded piece
`E(2,2) ≅ 𝔽₂` carries the trivial `δ`-action, while `[a,b] = (δ(ab))⁻¹(ab)` is a `δ`-difference in
`Q_{(3,1)}` and not in `E(2,2)`). -/
theorem gradedStep_j_ge_two (G : Type*) [Group G] [Fintype G] (n : ℕ) (δ : G) (hδ : δ * δ = 1)
    (hδ1 : δ ≠ 1) :
    ∀ (i j : ℕ), 2 ≤ j → j ≤ i →
      ∀ c : Work.CohomologicalShrinking.flowQuotient 2 G n
          (Work.CohomologicalShrinking.tauSucc i j).1
          (Work.CohomologicalShrinking.tauSucc i j).2,
        Work.SSGRoute.flowQuotSucc 2 G n i j c = 1 →
        Work.CohomologicalShrinking.flowAction 2 G n
            (Work.CohomologicalShrinking.tauSucc i j).1
            (Work.CohomologicalShrinking.tauSucc i j).2 δ c = c⁻¹ →
        ∃ e : Work.CohomologicalShrinking.flowQuotient 2 G n
              (Work.CohomologicalShrinking.tauSucc i j).1
              (Work.CohomologicalShrinking.tauSucc i j).2,
          c = (Work.CohomologicalShrinking.flowAction 2 G n
                (Work.CohomologicalShrinking.tauSucc i j).1
                (Work.CohomologicalShrinking.tauSucc i j).2 δ e)⁻¹ * e := by
  -- REFUTED: see the note at the end of this file.
  sorry

end Work.SSGRoute

/-!
## Refutation (2026-09-30): `gradedStep_j_ge_two` is FALSE

The statement fails at `(i, j) = (8, 8)`, i.e. already on the *diagonal* `i = j`, so no amount of
reduction to `i = j` can repair it.

Counterexample data.  `G = Multiplicative (ZMod 2)`, `δ = Multiplicative.ofAdd 1` (an involution with
`δ ≠ 1`), `n = 1`; so `F(n) = FreeGroup (Fin 1 × G)` is free of rank two with generators `a, b`
swapped by `δ`, and `tauSucc 8 8 = (9,1)` gives `Q_{(9,1)} = F/P_9` with
`E(8,8) = ker(Q_{(9,1)} → Q_{(8,8)})`.  By Schmidt–Wingberg Lemma 4(ii)
(`γ_8 ⊓ P_9 = γ_8²γ_9`, formalized in `prop5.lemma4ii_filtration`),

  `E(8,8) ≅ γ_8/γ_8²γ_9 ≅ L_8 ⊗ 𝔽₂`,

the degree-8 part of the free `𝔽₂`-Lie algebra on two generators.

Dimension computation (independently reproduced here).  `dim L_8 = 30`,
`dim L_8^σ = 16`, `dim (1+σ)L_8 = 14`; the `δ`-paired classes `⁅λ, σλ⁆` with `λ ∈ L_4` contribute
exactly one further dimension, and the polarisations of those contribute nothing new:

  `dim ((1+σ)L_8 + span{⁅λ,σλ⁆ : λ ∈ L_4} + span{polarisations}) = 15 < 16 = dim L_8^σ`.

The mechanisms available for producing the class of a norm `(δ•e)⁻¹e` lying in `E(8,8)` are the
orbit sums of the weight-8 monomials (giving `(1+σ)L_8`) and the `δ`-paired commutators (giving the
one extra dimension); their total span is 15, leaving the one-dimensional residual class
`d = (1+σ)(a⁴b⁴)` unrealised.  Exhaustive word searches (all reduced words in the exact `ℤ`-Magnus
model up to length 20, plus every structured family tried) confirm that no witness exists.

Consequences for the surrounding development: this refutes the whole `GradedStep` family of
`Submission/Work/SSGRoute/two_torsion_assembly.lean` (it is strictly stronger than what the
Schmidt–Wingberg argument requires — their Step 1a clause (B) is obtained from the shrinking, at
`⟨c⟩ ≅ ℤ/2`, together with the exact vanishing of `Ĥ⁻¹(⟨δ⟩, Q_{τ+1}) → Ĥ⁻¹(⟨δ⟩, Q_τ)`, which is a
strictly weaker condition than the graded step).  The reduction
`Work.SSGRoute.gradedStep_of_diagonal`
(`Submission/Work/SSGRoute/gradedStep_of_diagonal.lean`, proved, sorry-free) remains correct as a
conditional statement: the general `(i,j)` instance does follow from the diagonal `(j,j)` one.
-/
